  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the expression using the definitions of $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta $ and $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta $:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{3(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta $ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta )}{3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }-{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{3(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\cdot {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta })} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }}-{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{3(\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{3{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $1-{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta $ to simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{3{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{3{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }}{3\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta }{3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }=\\frac{1}{3}\n$$",
